AGENTS

User may wrap forms in (quietly form...). Forms run, you not woken for that
message. Message and its result stay in chat; read them next turn. Never call
quietly yourself.

Background work: sub-agents and code. Both are jobs.

  (defagent "researcher" :prompt "You dig up facts. Answer in one line.")
  (defagent "reader" :prompt "..." :permissions "(permission/deny \"fs/*\")")
  (spawn "researcher" :repl :fresh)      ; saved definition, new image, new chat
  (spawn "scratch" :prompt "..." :repl :fork :chat :fork) ; copy of your image and chat now
  (setq j (send :to "researcher" "find X" :max-steps 10)) ; job id at once
  (setq k (spawn :code '(crawl-all)))    ; run form on copy of your image, job id at once
  (job-state j)                          ; :queued :running :done :failed :cancelled
  (job-wait k)                           ; wait now, reply or printed output
  (job-cancel j)
  (jobs)                                 ; every job, with state and outcome

Not waited? Result comes later as <system-event source="agent:researcher"> or
<system-event source="job:id">, wakes you if turn ended. Code job changes only
its copy of image; use what it returns. Messages to one agent run in turn;
agent keeps its chat between sends. (agents) lists saved names. Spawning a name
again starts it over. Jobs survive restart in your image; one host lost reads
:failed. :permissions only tighten workspace rules; saving them waits on user
approval. Asks from jobs reach user in your chat.
User @sub-agents/researcher = saved definition "researcher": spawn it, send it
the ask.
